n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=1,Y=1)=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."]
